==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Myrcia, type ξ''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Divine Myrcia ξ''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Myrcia's set of abilities is rather inconvenient. Multi-hit gets in the way of her ability to create [[Wave Attack|waves]], as the two hits are in quick succession, so the first prevents the second from landing if the enemy in question gets knocked back. Waves, then, get in the way of her dodge ability by clearing the weak peons that could keep the ability triggered. Despite all this, Myrcia can still be used as a general unit in stages that feature many [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies, where she can deliver decent base damage and wave damage, while protecting other units at the same time. Her inconsistent dodge ability, however, makes this unit not recommended to be relied upon on her own, especially in absence of Traitless peons to keep her dodge state active; it is especially important that peons are the ones activating her Dodge, as many Traitless enemies are tough pushers, including but not limited to the famed [[R.Ost]], [[Heavenly Tower]] bosses, and the [[:Category:Crazed Cat Stages|Crazed Cats/Manic Cat]]s. You can also use her for clearing peons with her wave attack, but still, this uber has little to no usage outside of her niche, so it's hard to find a way to use her successfully.

==='''True Form'''===
Divine Myrcia ξ gains doubled health and wave level. Unfortunately, the doubled health does not really change anything about her, due to her not gaining increased dodge chance, increased dodge duration, or increased knockback count. The doubled wave level, however, is both a blessing and a curse, she can now snipe more enemy backliners with her waves, but they will now also kill more traitless peons that could keep her dodge state active. There is no really good improvement in this True Form, one of them being largely irrelevant and the other being practically a double-edged sword. Therefore, it is recommended to spend your [[Catfruit]] on another unit, as there is no real need to unlock this form.

==='''Talents'''===
As a unit centered around an extremely unreliable ability, Myrcia's Talents are not worth any investment.

'''Attack Up''' and '''HP Up''' could theoretically work, but they bring little improvement on a unit that simply doesn't have the stats from the get-go.

'''Dodge Attack''' offers a miniscule increases. While 40% is fairly high, attacks that slip through will still remove her relatively quickly.

'''Curse Immunity''' is completely useless. The [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]] isn't that much of concern in many of its appearances alongside traitless enemies. [[Master Uril (Enemy)|Master Uril]] is the only valid target, but her compatibility is off by a long shot, as his extreme DPS will eat through her in seconds.

'''Immune to Surge''' does help on paper, given their prevalence, but Myrcia simply cannot compete with alternatives. [[Kappy Jr.]] is the only Traitless surge enemy she can outrange. The scope expands slightly on the likes of [[Medu-san]], but her range puts her at a rather awkward position compared to dedicated meatshields and attackers, to the point where dedicated meatshields and attackers are more viable. This would also help against [[Master Uril (Enemy)|Master Uril]], but just like Curse Immunity, this won't help alot, as even with both she is still gonna die quickly.

